   548	
   549	### 6.1 The flat per-node projection
   550	
   551	`project : tree → #{[id tag & slots]}`, one row per distinct subtree:
   552	
   553	- `id` is the subtree's address (§4.3);
   554	- `tag` is the node's tag;
   555	- a `node` slot holds the child's address; a `nodes` slot holds a vector of
   556	  child addresses; every other slot holds its data unchanged.
   557	
   558	Because a tag has one arity in the tree, it has one arity in the projection
   559	(arity plus one for the id). Rows of one tag are homogeneous, so a
   560	where-pattern for a tag has exactly that tag's arity and no padding. Rows
   561	from many trees union into one relation without collision, because ids are
   562	addresses. Identical subtrees collapse to one row; an occurrence count is
