   911	#### 7.7.3 The fixed point
   912	
   913	- **Parked ids.** Each extracted parked id must name a record in the
   914	  carried `:parked` slice (UCF §7.6.3); a missing one is `:yin.k/unsatisfied`
   915	  naming the id.
   916	- **Values.** Closures, streams, and cursors reachable from the frame, the
   917	  K frames, parked records, the store slice, and the pending wait
   918	  contribute segment addresses and stream identities as §7.6.1 specifies;
   919	  each newly reached address is fetched, validated, projected, and its rows
   920	  added to `$ast` or `$code` with the activation that reached it recorded
   921	  as the context of its obligations (§7.7.2), and the queries are re-run
   922	  until no new address appears.
   923	- **Modules.** A required module with an undeclared footprint sets
   924	  `:yin.k/discovery :incomplete`, as §7.6.1 already rules.
   925	
   926	Discovery is `:complete` only when every reachable address was fetched
   927	and validated, every obligation was discharged in its own context or
   928	retained as a profiled requirement, every parked id resolved, and every
   929	module footprint was declared. It is `:blocked` when an address cannot be
   930	fetched and `:incomplete` otherwise. Recasting the walk as Datalog changes
   931	where the facts come from, not the conservatism of the closure.
   932	
   933	Because the queries are over data, they answer for a tree that has never
   934	run, which is the property §7.6.1 names.
